---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<section class="g-section g-features" aria-labelledby="g-features-title">
  <div class="g-wrap">
    <h2 id="g-features-title" class="g-visually-hidden">What gournal does</h2>
    <div class="g-features__grid">
      <article class="g-tile">
        <pre class="g-tile__specimen" tabindex="0" aria-label="Example MCP call"><code><span class="t-dim">tools/call</span> add_entry
{ <span class="t-key">"summary"</span>: "Wrote retry tests",
  <span class="t-key">"project"</span>: "worker",
  <span class="t-key">"agent"</span>: "claude-code" }</code></pre>
        <h3>Agents log for you</h3>
        <p>
          Claude Code and other MCP clients add entries through the gournal MCP server as they finish work.
          <code>gournal setup claude</code> registers the server and installs the skill. An optional Stop hook reminds
          Claude to log.
        </p>
        <a class="g-tile__more" href={`${base}docs/guides/logging-with-ai-agents/`}>Logging with AI agents</a>
      </article>

      <article class="g-tile">
        <pre class="g-tile__specimen" tabindex="0" aria-label="Example blockers and next items"><code><span class="t-red">Blockers</span>
  <span class="t-dim">Nov 14</span>  Waiting on keys  <span class="t-acc">[api]</span>

<span class="t-yel">Next</span>
  <span class="t-dim">Nov 15</span>  Ship metrics  <span class="t-acc">[worker]</span></code></pre>
        <h3>Standups that write themselves</h3>
        <p>
          <code>gournal standup</code> groups today's done entries by project. Open blockers and next items carry
          forward until an entry resolves them. Ask for <code>--yesterday</code>, <code>--week</code>, or a date range.
        </p>
        <a class="g-tile__more" href={`${base}docs/guides/standups-and-work-logs/`}>Standups and work logs</a>
      </article>

      <article class="g-tile">
        <pre class="g-tile__specimen" tabindex="0" aria-label="Example linked pull request"><code><span class="t-dim">10:41</span>  Fixed token refresh race
       <span class="t-dim">↳ merged #412</span>
       <span class="t-dim">↳ 3 commits</span></code></pre>
        <h3>GitHub, linked</h3>
        <p>
          <code>gournal sync</code> reads your pull requests, commits, and reviews through the <code>gh</code> CLI. It
          links each item to an entry by PR number, commit sha, or branch and time. Items not linked to a done entry in the report go to the Also line.
        </p>
        <a class="g-tile__more" href={`${base}docs/guides/github-activity/`}>GitHub activity</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
